<title>UK: M.A.I.D. indicated higher on venture hopes.</title>
<headline>M.A.I.D. indicated higher on venture hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in M.A.I.D. were marked up 12-1/2p to 322-1/2 in pre-market dealings on a press report suggesting the UK online business information service may soon announce a joint venture with an American cable company, traders said.  </p>
<p>London's Daily Mail suggested American cable concern TCI Communications may be a likely partner for M.A.I.D.</p>
<p>The Daily Mail, quoting M.A.I.D. officials, said the company was not for sale. The comments were made in response to speculation and press reports that Reuters was poised to launch a bid for the company.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
